radcli
------------------------------------------
The radcli library is a library for writing RADIUS Clients. The library's
approach is to allow writing RADIUS-aware application in less than 50 lines of
C code. It was based originally on freeradius-client and radiusclient-ng and is
source compatible with them.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgnutls-devel-3.8.13-1
  libgnutls30-3.8.13-1
  libnettle-devel-4.0-1
  libnettle9-4.0-1
  libradcli-devel-2.0.1-1bl1
  libradcli10-2.0.1-1bl1
  libradcli2-devel-2.0.1-1bl1
  libradcli2_1-2.0.1-1bl1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libgnutls-devel-3.8.13-1
  libnettle-devel-4.0-1
  meson-1.10.2-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/radcli/radcli

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/radcli/radcli/archive/refs/tags/2.0.1.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack radcli-2.0.1-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./radcli-2.0.1-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/radcli-2.0.1-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/radcli-2.0.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libradcli10-2.0.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libradcli2_1-2.0.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libradcli-devel-2.0.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libradcli2-devel-2.0.1-X.tar.xz

